DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     Increment the _v___u_s_e_c_o_u_n_t field of a vnode.

     _v_p  the vnode to increment

     Each vnode maintains a reference count of how many parts of the system
     are using the vnode.  This allows the system to detect when a vnode is no
     longer being used and can be safely recycled for a different file.

     Any code in the system which is using a vnode (e.g. during the operation
     of some algorithm or to store in a data structure) should call vvrreeff() or
     vvrreeffll().

     vvrreeff() locks the vnode interlock while vvrreeffll() expects the interlock to
     already be held.

